# Board 0.26, F69 (the product owner's ruling of 2026-10-15): a dock takes nobody out of view.
# Story: the welcome coach's own first two keys. An editor that will not go under 1188 points goes left, a mail app that will not go under
# 760 goes right, on a display 1920 wide. Side by side they need 1948 and there are 1896, and halves do not help. macOS alone would let
# them overlap and hide nothing. So does Arbor: room first, and for what is still missing they overlap. Each keeps its place in
# the arrangement, flush with the outer side of its place: the editor at its smallest, the mail app in the half its key asked for, which it is
# not made to give up for one that does not fit anyway. The window the key named lies in front.
display-size 1920x1080
open Editor 1300x800 min 1188x685
open Mail 1000x680 min 760x400
focus 101
press dock left
expect visible 101
focus 102
press dock right
# Nobody has left.
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect count docked 2
# Flush left at its smallest; the right half.
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 1188x1031
expect at 102 966 37
expect size 102 942x1031
expect in-front 102
expect focused 102
expect said Too wide to stand side by side · they overlap
# Which lies in front later is macOS's business: a click or ⌘Tab brings the editor forward, and moves and sizes nothing.
focus 101
expect still
expect in-front 101
# One step back: the mail app floats where it was, and the editor has the room.
undo
expect floating 102
expect at 102 300 200
expect size 102 1000x680
# It ends by itself when something else gives the room: docked again, then the editor closes.
redo
expect at 101 12 37
expect size 101 1188x1031
expect at 102 966 37
close 101
expect visible 102
